@* A cell holding a list, kept to exactly one line: the first item is rendered inline (clipped rather than
   wrapped) and the rest sit behind a "+n more" affordance that opens the whole set in a dialog. Every
   virtualised row is one line, because the virtualiser positions rows arithmetically from a single fixed
   ItemSize, so a chip per item from a @foreach is a row that grows with its data.

   This generalises the affordance the Connected System Object's attribute grid already carries, so a call site
   supplies only what is particular to it: the items, how one of them is drawn, and what to call them. The
   dialog draws each item with the SAME template, so chips stay chips and links stay clickable; a tooltip
   listing the rest would have flattened both. *@

@* The items are captured by the pattern rather than dereferenced through a guard, per the nullable-dereference
   rule in JIM.Web/CLAUDE.md: a pattern guard does not satisfy CodeQL, a local bound by one does. *@
@if (Items is { Count: > 0 } items)
{
    <div class="jim-one-line-list">
        <span class="jim-one-line-list-value">@ItemTemplate(items[0])</span>
        @if (items.Count > 1)
        {
            <MudButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" Class="jim-attr-expand-btn" OnClick="OpenAllAsync">
                +@((items.Count - 1).ToString("N0")) more
            </MudButton>
        }
    </div>
}
else if (EmptyContent != null)
{
    @EmptyContent
}
else
{
    <EmptyValue />
}

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The items the cell holds. The first is shown; the rest are reachable through the affordance.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<TItem>? Items { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// How one item is drawn, inline and in the dialog alike.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public RenderFragment<TItem> ItemTemplate { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>
    /// What the items are, as a plural noun ("Roles", "Object Types", "Sources"). It titles the dialog and is
    /// counted in it ("3 Roles").
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// What to render when there are no items at all. Defaults to the <see cref="EmptyValue"/> placeholder;
    /// pass something where the emptiness itself means something the reader should be told ("Not assigned").
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public RenderFragment? EmptyContent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// The dialog states its own height ceiling rather than the shared grid's footer measurement, because its
    /// container is not the page: the measurement would describe the page behind the overlay.
    /// </summary>
    private static readonly DialogOptions Options = new() { FullWidth = true, MaxWidth = MaxWidth.Small, CloseButton = true };

    private async Task OpenAllAsync()
    {
        var items = Items;
        if (items == null)
            return;

        var parameters = new DialogParameters<OverflowListDialog<TItem>>
        {
            { x => x.Items, items },
            { x => x.ItemTemplate, ItemTemplate },
            { x => x.Title, Title }
        };

        await DialogService.ShowAsync<OverflowListDialog<TItem>>(Title, parameters, Options);
    }
}
